        "question_BxwcyQ": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What’s the difference between threadless and internally threaded flatbacks?",
            "answer": "<ul><li><strong>Threadless flatbacks</strong> use a tension-fit post and pin system. The decorative end slides into the post and stays secure through pressure, making them easy to insert and remove without<br/>twisting.</li><li><strong>Internally threaded flatbacks</strong> have<br/>a post with internal threads and a screw-on top, ensuring a very secure fit and<br/>smooth insertion.</li></ul><p>Both options provide a secure, professional-grade hold — the choice depends on<br/>personal preference or studio standards.</p>",
            "icon": "none"
          }
        },
        "question_XwGzDp": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": " How do I know the gold is authentic?",
            "answer": "<p>All our gold jewellery is genuine 14K solid gold and quality-checked before shipment. Each item meets strict purity standards and contains a gold hallmark for authenticity. We also have certificates upon customers’ request for all our items.</p>",
            "icon": "none"
          }
        },
        "question_8bHeMB": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": " How should I care for my gold body jewellery?",
            "answer": "<p>Clean your 14K gold jewellery with mild soap and warm water, then gently dry with a soft cloth. Avoid harsh chemicals or abrasive cloths to maintain its shine. Store your pieces in a dry place to prevent scratching.</p>",
            "icon": "none"
          }
        },
        "question_p9HaqG": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What piercing types can flatbacks be used for?",
            "answer": "<p>Gold flatbacks are suitable for a variety of piercings including helix, tragus, conch, lobe, lip, and cartilage piercings. Their flat base makes them especially comfortable for areas where jewellery sits close to the skin.</p>",
            "icon": "none"
          }
